\title{Matching set cardinalities}
\date{2026-03-12T13:50:08Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{Let #{A}, #{B} be sets. If there exists a [bijection](00AF) #{f : A \to B} then we say #{A} and #{B} have the same cardinality, and write #{|A| = |B|}.}
\p{If there is an injection #{f : A \to B} then we say #{|A| \leq |B|}.}
